    <briefdescription>
<para>A Rectified Linear Unit activation layer. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1ReLU" kindref="compound">ReLU</ref> class implements the <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1ReLU" kindref="compound">ReLU</ref> activation function as a network layer, applying the elementwise transformation:   <formula id="92">\[    f(x) = \max(0, x)
\]</formula> to the input tensor during the forward pass. The input tensor and its shape are stored internally for reference. This layer contains no learnable parameters.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1Layer" kindref="compound">Layer</ref> for the base class from which this class derives. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1TensorView_1a944f540504a95bbc578d627140307110" kindref="member">TensorView::ReLU()</ref> for the underlying tensor operation that performs the elementwise <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1ReLU" kindref="compound">ReLU</ref> computation and constructs the computational graph node. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
